  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760295,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1988: A Presidential Challenge for the Commodore 64\n\nStep into the political arena with *1988*, a compelling election simulation for the Commodore 64, updated from the earlier *President Elect*. This game plunges you into the heart of the 1988 United States presidential race, challenging you to navigate the complexities of campaigning and policy-making.\n\nAssume the role of a presidential candidate and embark on a quest for the White House. You'll need to craft a winning platform, manage your finances, and rally support across key states.  Address critical issues like the economy, defense, and social welfare, carefully considering how your stances will impact voter opinion. \n\nThe game features a dynamic election system where your decisions directly influence public perception and your opponent's strategies.  Manage your campaign team, participate in debates, and respond to unexpected events – all while striving to secure enough electoral votes to claim victory.  Can you master the art of political maneuvering and become the next President of the United States?  *1988* offers a surprisingly deep and engaging experience for strategy enthusiasts."
    },
